# {{TITLE_RAW}}

Generated with **Zevui Initializr** (Zig {{ZIG_VERSION_RAW}} / DVUI + SDL3).

This is a standalone Zig project; no Zevui CLI or Python is needed to build.

The generated `mise.toml` pins Zig {{ZIG_VERSION_RAW}}. `mise install` and
`mise exec -- zig build` are optional conveniences, **not** build requirements.
Without mise, install Zig {{ZIG_VERSION_RAW}} and verify `zig version` before building.

```sh
zig build
zig build run
zig build -Dportable-gui=true
```

SQLite3 is opt-in and uses the system SQLite library by default. Select a link mode:

```sh
zig build test -Dsqlite=system         # requires system sqlite3 development library
zig build test -Dsqlite=off            # no C symbols and no libc from this addon
python3 src/addons/sqlite_vendor.py    # one-time verified official SQLite bootstrap
zig build test -Dsqlite=bundled        # compiles the checked vendor source
```

The vendor script is optional and uses Python 3 only for the explicit one-time download.
No Python or Node is needed for ordinary Zig builds. The SQLite code is isolated
from Zevui core. `-Dsqlite=bundled` requires the generated C source to be present.
Do not use `-Dsqlite=system` if the system development library is missing; on
Windows prefer bundled after vendoring. Initializr selection currently supports Linux
only; Windows/macOS remain gated on native tests. The copied MIT notice for
the Zig wrapper is at `src/addons/sqlite_LICENSE.txt`.

